    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Build succeeds and both acceptance tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nOwner deletion is now a soft-delete. Changes made:\n\n**Entity & persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `deleted` field (`Boolean`, column `deleted`, defaulting to `FALSE`) with getter/setter, so a newly created owner is `deleted=false`.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added a `deleted` column (`DEFAULT FALSE` / `DEFAULT 0` for MySQL) to the `owners` table.\n\n**Endpoint behavior**\n- `rest/function/owner/DeleteOwner.java` \u2014 instead of `repository.delete(owner)`, it now sets `deleted=true` and saves, retaining the row. The DELETE pipeline still responds `204` (2xx). `GET /api/owners/{id}` continues to load the retained row via `findById`, now returning `deleted=true`.\n\n**API contract**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct maps it automatically (shown as `$.deleted` in GET responses).\n\n**Create-time duplicate/identity checks now ignore deleted owners**\n- `RejectDuplicateIdentity` (the 409 household-duplicate block), `FlagPossibleDuplicate` (soft-duplicate signal), `CountOwnerNamesakes` (name identity count), and `CountHouseholdMembers` (household size) all skip owners flagged `deleted`. So a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` both green, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\nI left capacity/quota checks (`RejectCityAtCapacity`, `RejectOverDailyLimit`) unchanged, since the specification scoped the exclusion to \"duplicate and identity checks.\"",
